cut Command: to cut the output and display spacefic word  

1)to display one word word
cut -c1 fileame
2) dispay two word
cut -c1,3 filename
3) display range of word
cut -c1-3 filename
4) display word from specific output
ls -l | cut -c1
5) display the filed without delimator like :
cut -d: -f 3 directory or file (example: /etc/passwd)

awk command: Display spacefic filed

1) to display 1 or 2 filed 
awk '{print $2,$3}' filename
2) to display last colum
awk '{print $NF}' filename
3) to display file content with serial number
awk '{print NR $0}' filename
4) to display file content with serial number and then space
awk '{print NR, $0}' filename
5) to display file content with serial number and colon space
awk '{print NR ": " $0}' filename
6) to display filed when dont have space between the filed
awk -F, '{print $1}' passwd
7) condition: when you want to display salary which is grater than 10000
awk '{if($4>10000) print $0}' filename


grep command: to display specific keyword 

1)to display one keyword
grep keyword filename

2) to display keword from the file stre under directory ( you can use any command od below both)
cat /etc/passwd | grep tejas
grep tejas /etc/passwd

3) other use of grep
grep -i keyword filename ( reguraly use this case sensitie)
grep -n keyword filename ( to check keyword with feild no)
grep -c keyword filename ( to check how may times specific kewords comes in perticular file)
grep -v keyword filename  ( it display all other keyword escape mentioned in command)

4) egrep command
egrep "first keyword|second keyword" filename (to check two keyword at time)
